= Solution
{parent=a}

A <Poisson process> has a <Poisson distribution> for the count in an interval of length $t$, with mean equal to rate times length. Fifteen minutes is $1/4$ hour, so
$$
\boxed{N(5{:}15)-N(5{:}00)\sim\operatorname{Poisson}(3),\qquad\mathbb P(N=k)=e^{-3}\frac{3^k}{k!},\quad k\geq0.}
$$

= b
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The first arrival time $T_1$, measured in hours after opening, has <exponential distribution> of rate twelve. Therefore
$$
\boxed{\mathbb P(1/4<T_1<1/2)=e^{-12/4}-e^{-12/2}=e^{-3}-e^{-6}.}
$$
Equivalently, there must be no arrivals in the first quarter hour and at least one in the next; <independent increments> give $e^{-3}(1-e^{-3})$.

= c
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=c}

Let $I_2=T_2-T_1$ and $I_3=T_3-T_2$ be the interarrival times adjacent to the second arrival. They are independent <exponential random variables> of rate twelve per hour. The second customer meets the first if $I_2<1/12$ hour, and meets a later customer if $I_3<1/12$ hour. If the third arrives too late, every subsequent customer does also. Thus the only way to meet nobody is for both gaps to be at least five minutes:
$$
\mathbb P(\text{no meeting})=\mathbb P(I_2\geq1/12)\mathbb P(I_3\geq1/12)=e^{-1}e^{-1}=e^{-2}.
$$
Hence $\boxed{\mathbb P(\text{meeting})=1-e^{-2}}$. Exact equality of arrival and departure times has <probability> zero. The calculation includes both customers already present and customers arriving during the visit; it is a <two-sided interarrival test for overlap>.

= d
{parent=1}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=d}

Independent marking with <probability> $5/6$ is <Poisson thinning> and gives a <Poisson process> of chip-buying arrivals, of rate $12(5/6)=10$ per hour. Its first arrival time therefore satisfies
$$
\boxed{T_{\rm chips}\sim\operatorname{Exp}(10\text{ per hour}),\qquad\mathbb E T_{\rm chips}=\frac1{10}\text{ hour}=6\text{ minutes}.}
$$
For example, its survival <probability> is $\mathbb E[(1/6)^{N(t)}]=\exp(12t(1/6-1))=e^{-10t}$, which also derives the thinning conclusion directly.

= 2
{parent=M}
